  "id": "musica_chapaca_tarija",
  "name": "Música chapaca (Tarija valley seasonal music)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Music of the chapacos, the country people of the Tarija valley in southern Bolivia, whose instruments follow the festive calendar: the erke, a cow horn sounded through a thin cane tube with a reed, played with the caja at Carnival; the caña, a long cane trumpet heard at the Fiesta de San Roque with its chunchos dancers; the violín chapaco; and the camacheña cane flute. The caja, a shallow double-headed drum struck with a single beater, also accompanies women's sung coplas. The horns card stands in for the erke and caña and the bamboo-flute card for the camacheña.",
  "recipe": "classic modern música chapaca, carnival Processional, andean branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment, single lead single track no stacking. credited horns bamboo credited bamboo flute unspecified, fiddle, membrane drum pulse resonant acoustic membrane drum. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
